; A Value:: tag on one posting values every other amount of the same lot
; too: Assets:Retirement, whose purchase carries no tag, is worth $70
; under -V, at the $7 a unit of Assets:Broker's tag ($70 for 10 units),
; not the $50 its own purchase price gives.
;
; This is Ledger's long-standing behaviour, kept on purpose: a valuation
; belongs to the lot rather than to the posting that brings it, and every
; amount of the lot, in any account, carries it.  The same sharing lets a
; balance assertion, an automated transaction and a sale see the lot
; whole (the other lot-value-expr-*.test files).  3.4.1 shared the
; valuation the same way but read the tag's $70 as $70 a unit (#2399),
; so each account's 10 AAPL was worth $700 under -V.

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker        10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]  ; Value:: $70
    Assets:Cash         $-50

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Retirement    10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
    Assets:Cash         $-50

test bal --lots
                             $-100
20 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Broker
               $-100    Cash
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Retirement
--------------------
                             $-100
20 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))
end test

test bal -V
                 $40  Assets
                 $70    Broker
               $-100    Cash
                 $70    Retirement
--------------------
                 $40
end test
